DirkuLator 0.5.4rc: position invariance (from nxnative #1673 / #1789 for OoT's EQUAL depth passes). Geometry stages
(vertex, tessellation, geometry, task, mesh) decorate every float add/mul/fma NoContraction; vertex Position and the
mesh-emulation vertex shader's Position are Invariant. Fragment/compute unchanged. Translator salt bumped.

diff --git a/src/shader_recompiler/backend/spirv/emit_spirv_floating_point.cpp b/src/shader_recompiler/backend/spirv/emit_spirv_floating_point.cpp
--- a/src/shader_recompiler/backend/spirv/emit_spirv_floating_point.cpp
+++ b/src/shader_recompiler/backend/spirv/emit_spirv_floating_point.cpp
@@ -11,7 +11,11 @@
 namespace {
 Id Decorate(EmitContext& ctx, IR::Inst* inst, Id op) {
     const auto flags{inst->Flags<IR::FpControl>()};
-    if (flags.no_contraction) {
+    // 0.5.4: geometry stages compute positions that other programs must match bit for bit (a depth
+    // pre-pass and an EQUAL colour pass drawn by different programs), so none of their float math
+    // is contracted or reordered by the host compiler.
+    const bool geometry{ctx.stage != Stage::Fragment && ctx.stage != Stage::Compute};
+    if (flags.no_contraction || geometry) {
         ctx.Decorate(op, spv::Decoration::NoContraction);
     }
     return op;
